.TH PLANK-TABLET-RELAY-BLE 1 "September 2026" "PLANK" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plank-tablet-relay-ble \- Bluetooth tablet readings relay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plank-tablet-relay-ble
.RI [ --config " file" ]
.RI [ --check-config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publishes PLANK Tablet Setup's Bluetooth LE service and reads qualifying
Wacom pen and tablet-button input through Linux input devices.
The headset approves its first connection using three tablet-button presses;
subsequent connections authenticate the saved keys.
Normally run through the plank-tablet-relay-ble system service.
The headset app can discover and pair a tablet on an unconfigured relay.
Subsequent tablet management requires an approved headset.
The relay hostname is advertised by default; configuration may override it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Read the specified configuration instead of the system default.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate configuration and exit without opening Bluetooth or tablet devices.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/plank-tablet-relay-ble/relay.conf
Adapter, tablet selection and opt-in controller compatibility settings.
.TP
.I /var/lib/plank-tablet-relay-ble
Private identity, approved headset keys, tablet selection and pairing attempt budget.
Retained by package upgrades, removal and purge.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/plank-tablet-relay-ble/linux-ble-package.md.gz
Installation, hardware qualification and compatibility guidance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR plank-tablet-relay-admin (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1)
